# The disposable-copy profile, read by `npm run dev:web:qa`.
#
# Overlaid on .env, so it states only what differs: a DIFFERENT database and
# the write gate open. Copy this to `.env.qa` — which is gitignored, because it
# carries a connection string — and create the database it names.
#
# Why this file exists at all: writes are never enabled against the live
# corpus. This project has corrupted its own data twice through "it's only a
# test" writes, and a browser session is not covered by the vitest real-data
# guard. `npm run dev` cannot write no matter what is clicked; this profile can,
# against a copy nobody minds losing.
#
# Creating and seeding the copy, from the repo root:
#
#   docker exec scraplify-postgres-1 createdb -U scraplify scraplify_qa
#   docker exec scraplify-postgres-1 sh -c \
#     'pg_dump -U scraplify scraplify | psql -U scraplify scraplify_qa'
#
# Re-seed it whenever the live corpus has moved on enough to matter. It is a
# copy, not a mirror, and nothing keeps the two in step.

DATABASE_URL=postgres://scraplify:scraplify_dev@127.0.0.1:5432/scraplify_qa
XTELO_WRITES_ENABLED=true
